  "id": "consummatory-pleasure",
  "term": "consummatory pleasure",
  "definition": "Consummatory pleasure is the enjoyment a person feels in the present moment while an event or activity is happening. It is described as a distinct part of hedonic experience, separate from anticipatory pleasure, which concerns expected future enjoyment.",
